  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Reppe and Destel gorges meet north of Ollioules, carved by water into beautiful white limestone. The listed site served as a hideout for the 18th-century bandit Gaspard de Besse. "Gorges d'Ollioules" usually means the main road running through them; the Destel gorges are the wild site reachable only on foot.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p><strong>Dogs:</strong> the Provence Méditerranée tourist office says "animals accepted" and describes a sporty, difficult trail with a steep elevation change. It publishes no leash rule; on ground with chains and pothole crossings, a short leash is the safest option.</p>
      <p><strong>Route:</strong> park at the small dog-club car park on the RN8, about 1 km after leaving Ollioules towards Sainte-Anne d'Évenos, cross the Reppe, then follow the Destel streambed up to the potholes (natural pools). Chains and handrails help in the hard sections. The hiking loop with the Château du Diable takes 2h30 to 3h30 according to Visorando (hiking shoes required, no drinking water).</p>
      <p><strong>Water and heat:</strong> the canyon is often dry in summer and only has water in late winter and early spring; don't count on the pools to cool your dog in high season. A local hiker advises bringing water in summer as it gets very hot in the potholes.</p>
      <p><strong>Forest massifs:</strong> per the tourist office, they are closed to vehicles from 15 June to 15 September (possibly extended to 30 September) and access can be banned to walkers in case of very severe or extreme fire risk; the Var prefecture publishes the massif status every day before 7pm for the next day.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a real good find if you're based in Toulon, outside summer and with a dog comfortable on rough terrain.</div>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> massif status in summer, whether the potholes hold water, and the lack of a published leash rule for the site.</p>
      <p>Sources read on 06/11/2026: <a href="https://www.provencemed.com/activite/gorges-dollioules-et-le-destel">Provence Méditerranée tourist office</a>, <a href="https://actu.fr/provence-alpes-cote-d-azur/evenos_83053/a-20-min-de-toulon-ces-gorges-spectaculaires-cachent-le-repaire-d-un-bandit-legendaire_64161303.html">actu.fr (18/04/2026)</a>, Visorando, Randonneurs du 13.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Ollioules, with its Provençal market, is a good stop before or after the outing.</p>
